    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always had a casual relationship with math—more as a tool than a passion. My upper secondary education gave me basics, and I’ve used math in practical tasks like budgeting or designing layouts. I don’t see it as a subject I deeply love, but I respect its logic and structure. It’s not central to my daily life, but I appreciate how it underpins many real-world decisions.",
